  "question": "Let $\\vec{a} = 3\\hat{i} - 2\\hat{j} + 4\\hat{k}$ and $\\vec{b} = \\hat{i} + 4\\hat{j} - 2\\hat{k}$. Find the value of $\\lambda$ such that $\\vec{a} + \\lambda \\vec{b}$ is perpendicular to $\\vec{a} - \\lambda \\vec{b}$.",
  "answeroption": "C",
  "explanation": "Let $\\vec{u} = \\vec{a} + \\lambda \\vec{b}$ and $\\vec{v} = \\vec{a} - \\lambda \\vec{b}$<br /><br />Perpendicularity:<br /><br />$\\vec{u} \\cdot \\vec{v} = 0$<br /><br />$[\\vec{a} + \\lambda \\vec{b}] \\cdot [\\vec{a} - \\lambda \\vec{b}] = 0$<br /><br />$\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{a} - \\lambda^2 \\vec{b} \\cdot \\vec{b} = 0$<br /><br />Thus $\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{a} = \\lambda^2 \\vec{b}\\cdot\\vec{b}$<br /><br />$\\implies \\lambda^2 = \\dfrac{\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{a}}{\\vec{b}\\cdot\\vec{b}}$<br /><br />$\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{a} = 9 + 4 + 16 = 29$<br /><br />$\\vec{b} \\cdot \\vec{b} = 1 + 16 + 4 = 21$<br /><br />$\\lambda^2 = 29/21$, so $\\lambda = \\pm \\sqrt{\\dfrac{29}{21}}$",
  "explanation_image": [],
